    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "nEW YORK\nmOnTREAL\nBURLINGTON\nCCA\nLaunk\nCANADIAN\nCOLONIAL\nAIRWAYS\nBe there rather than On Your Way",
      "CCA\nNEW YORK\n*\nMONTREAL\nTICKETS\nAIR TICKETS\nAND\nRESERVATIONS\nON ALL AIRLINES\nAIRLINES TICKET AGENCY\nOF E. K. SMITH, Inc. - 41 E. 42nd ST.\nVAnderbilt 6-0100\nGENERAL INFORMATION\nSTOPOVERS:\nare permitted\nproviding arrangements are\nmade in advance.\nCANCELLATION: The carrier may cancel any trip at origin\nor at any point and may omit any schedule\nbility in such event being limited to a refund of the unused\nmileage proportion of the fare paid.\nREFUNDS: The carrier will refund the fare upon surrender\nunused ticket three hours prior to scheduled departure\nof plane.\nIn event of flight cancellation or interruption, the\ncarrier will furnish refund draft or forwarding transportation\nvia suriace means to ticket destination.\nCAB SERVICE: Passengers desiring cabs at\nshould inform agent at station\nof departure.\ndestination\nCabs will be\nready upon arrival at destination.\nLOST ARTICLES: Inquiries\nregarding lost articles\nshould be\ndirected to the Lost and Found Dept.,\nCCA -\nNew\nYork\nTRIP INSURANCE: Trip insurance may be purchased at CCA\nticket and airport offices.\nBAGGAGE: Forty pounds of baggage will be carried free\non each ticket.\nBaggage in excess\nof 40 pounds will be\ncharged for at the rate\nof one-half of 1% of the published\none-way fare per pound.\nBaggage dimension limits\n54 x 24 x 20 or 60 x 24 x 19.\nTRANSOCEANIC PASSENGERS: See Ticket Agent for bag-\ngage allowance\ngranted Transoceanic Pan\nAmerican Air-\nways or Imperial\nAirways passengers to Bermuda.\nCUSTOMS: The usual immigration and customs inspection\nwill be made at St. Hubert Airport,\nBurlington Municipal and New York Airports,\nsouthbound\nGoods valued at not more than one hundred dollars ($100.00)\nand purchased by a person who is a resident and has been\nEntering Conta purchases over 85.00 must be declared tin\nCanada purchases\nover $5.00 must be declared\nwriting.\nEntering the U.\n. A. the same will apply to pur-\nchases over $25.00.\nYour Stewardess will gladly assist you.\nPrinted in U.S.A."
    ],
